<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Milner's Kindergarten</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Milner's Kindergarten was the name given to a group of young Oxford-educated administrators recruited by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-milner">Alfred Milner</a>, British High Commissioner in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, to rebuild the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-river">Orange River</a> colonies after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a>. Members such as Lionel Curtis, Philip Kerr and Patrick Duncan worked for the union of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> in 1910 and later founded the Round Table movement, which promoted closer imperial union.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/milners-kindergarten.jpg" alt="Milner's Kindergarten" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Duffus Brothers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Photograph_of_Lord_Milner_in_1902.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
